    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.168": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Advancement",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Advancement - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Administrative Assistant, Advancement University Relations Competition No. 26.07.168 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Non-Recurring Term (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date A review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Administrative Assistant, Advancement for a full-time, 6-month non-recurring term opportunity with our University Relations department. You will provide comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support to the Advancement portfolio. In this role, you will coordinate office operations, gift administration, meetings, recruitment activities, departmental projects, and advancement initiatives. You will also provide administrative support for donor stewardship, constituent record management, fundraising reporting, and advancement events while ensuring accuracy, confidentiality, and compliance with University policies and procedures. Key responsibilities include: Serving as the first point of contact for visitors, students, donors, alumni, and internal stakeholders by providing professional, courteous, and confidential customer service or redirecting requests to the appropriate staff member or department; Preparing, formatting, proofreading, and editing, correspondence, reports, presentations, proposals, gift agreements, and other documentation for review and approval while ensuring accuracy and adherence to university standards; Coordinating calendars, meetings and appointments for leadership and departmental staff; Assisting with planning departmental events, recognition activities and meetings, including preparing agendas and minutes, booking rooms and other logistics; Coordinating travel arrangements and travel expense documentation; Maintaining office supplies, promotional merchandise, equipment and coordinating repairs; Processing mail, courier requests, parking pass administration and other departmental memberships and professional association renewals; Assisting with SharePoint administration, records organization and document management; Processing cheque, cash, e-transfer, wire transfer, and Gift-in-Kind donation documentation in accordance with established procedures; Preparing and reconciling purchase requisitions, invoices, P-Card transactions and expense documentation; Maintaining and tracking records of stewardship activities, constituent and donor records in Raiser's Edge and updating Raiser's Edge in accordance with established procedures; Managing the Advancement shared email inboxes and voicemail, responding to routine inquiries and directing requests to the appropriate staff member; Providing administrative support for donor stewardship activities, alumni engagement initiatives, MMB tours, fundraising campaigns, annual giving initiatives and other related activities; and Assisting with recruitment activities including posting support, interview scheduling, candidate communications, onboarding and offboarding activities and payroll/human resource documentation. Skills You will have: Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines; Strong attention to detail and accuracy in preparing documentation, maintaining records, and processing financial and donor information; Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills with a strong customer service orientation; The ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with donors, alumni, senior leaders, and internal stakeholders; The ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion, and confidentiality when handling sensitive information; Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and implement appropriate solutions; The ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment; Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and the ability to learn and utilize systems such as Raiser's Edge, PeopleSoft, and SharePoint; Strong administrative and coordination skills, including meeting and event coordination, records management, recruitment support, and financial administration; and The initiative, adaptability, and the ability to respond effectively to changing priorities in a fast-paced environment. Qualifications A minimum of a 2-year post-secondary diploma in business administration, office administration, administrative professional, public administration, or a related field. Minimum 3 years of progressively responsible administrative experience supporting senior leaders or complex business operations, Experience with financial administration, recruitment coordination, records management, event coordination, and confidential administrative support. Experience supporting advancement, alumni relations, donor administration, or a comparable customer relationship management environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.204": {
      "title": "Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Admissions Assistant - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Admissions Assistant Office of the University Registrar Competition No. 26.08.204 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 17, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band C (Steps 1-8): $24.256 - $35.273 per hour. $44,147 - $64,197 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 17, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Admissions Assistant for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Office of the University Registrar. The position is an integral member of the Admissions team and is accountable for providing exemplary service, preparing admission files for evaluation, and providing support to the admission team. You will receive, organize, and manage related information and documentation to prepare a file for admission evaluation. Additionally, you will respond to future students, applicants, and parents regarding a broad range of inquiries related to applicant file status, admissions and transfer policies, procedures, and documentation requirements. Key responsibilities include: Entering applications and supporting documents (i.e. transcripts, test scores) into the student information system; Identifying and confirming receipt of academic transcripts and related admission documentation required for the evaluation of applications, and, where required, scanning and uploading to the electronic document management system and student record; Reviewing academic transcripts and applicable admission documents to verify authenticity and completeness, using multiple resources; Providing accurate admission information to future students, applicants, parents, and stakeholders by email or other electronic communication tools; Assisting applicants in understanding their admission and transfer credit statuses; Engaging with the Admissions team to ensure accurate and consistent information is provided to applicants, students, and staff; Identifying and recommending new or revised procedures where efficiencies can be optimized; and Assisting with and supporting the collaborative training model for new and existing employees. Skills You will have: Excellent written and verbal communication skills; A service-oriented approach with the ability to serve diverse prospective students, applicants, and other stakeholders with empathy, professionalism, clarity, consistency and conciseness; The ability to perform intermediate-level tasks using a student information system; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), SharePoint, Google and other software applications; The ability to organize time and priorities with limited supervision to meet goals and objectives; The ability to understand and anticipate applicants need using critical thinking and problem-solving skills; The ability to process large volumes of work and meet deadlines; Aptitude for accuracy and thoroughness with keen attention to detail; The ability to demonstrate flexibility and adaptability in a dynamic environment; and The ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Qualifications A minimum of a Diploma (two-year) with a focus on records/data management, administration or related areas. A minimum of one (1) year of administrative support and/or data management experience in program evaluation settings. Experience in a post-secondary institution in an administrative setting would be considered an asset. Knowledge of PeopleSoft - Campus Solutions would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
