    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers - MacEwan University",
      "description": "Careers - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About Careers About MacEwan Careers In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers In This Section Through teaching, supporting students and keeping our campus running smoothly, MacEwan University employees make a difference in the lives of our students. When you work here, you join a friendly and welcoming team that genuinely cares. Together, we deliver an exceptional undergraduate experience that inspires and empowers our students. Located in the heart of Edmonton, our energetic campus provides plenty of opportunities for making connections. Explore our job opportunities and take the first step toward a career you love. Why work here A welcoming community Relationships matter at MacEwan. Join a team that cares in a place where everyone belongs. Our people come first. Balance you can count on Generous vacation time, an annual holiday break, a focus on work-life balance. We know that life is about more than work. Opportunities to grow You can thrive at MacEwan through opportunities to sharpen your skills, advance your career and make a difference. MacEwan is a top employer In 2026, MacEwan University was named one of Alberta’s top employers. See why we’ve been selected We love working here Find out what makes working at MacEwan University so special from some of our faculty and staff. Troy Donovan “My beekeeping started with a hallway chat—I was curious about bees, and MacEwan was looking to start a hive. Next thing I know I’m working on this cool project, which wouldn’t have been possible without MacEwan’s efforts to make it possible.” Cyber Security Analyst Resident Urban Beekeeper Troy Donovan Neetu Sharma Chandelle Rimmer Molie Bigirimana News worth sharing Campus Life How Hana Matova helps construct community From classroom renovations to new buildings, the senior project manager of infrastructure is helping shape the future of our campus. June 30, 2026 Full Story Campus Life MacEwan welcomes new associate vice-president, Entrepreneurship Alumna Kassie Burkholder to build bridges between teaching excellence, innovation and community impact. June 29, 2026 Full Story Arts & Culture, Campus Life Office Hours: Soni Dasmohapatra nurtures honest discussion 2025 Early Career Teaching Excellence Award recipient shares her welcoming office space and some of her favourite research projects. April 20, 2026 Full Story 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Load More How Hana Matova helps construct community MacEwan welcomes new associate vice-president, Entrepreneurship Office Hours: Soni Dasmohapatra nurtures honest discussion “It’s really beautiful to watch students grow.” “Helping a student make an informed decision is what I treasure the most in this role.” Office hours: Dr. Melissa Hills takes student feedback to heart MacEwan welcomes new associate vice-president, Government and Community Relations MacEwan recognized as a top employer – again! Office Hours: For Dr. Lori Harper, it’s all about being grounded Office Hours: Robert Andruchow’s teaching is rooted in the real world “There are always people who need help.” Office Hours: Colin Waugh’s “un-office” “I quickly learned how difficult managing clothing can be when you experience disability.” Office Hours: Snacks and floor chats with Christine Pope “This is my dream job! It's a mix of what I love the most.” “It’s important for us to be passionate about what we’re doing.” Dr. Christy Raymond reappointed as dean of the Faculty of Nursing “It feels like making 9,000 new best friends.” Office hours: How one lab space guided Cody Esih’s journey Portrait: Kairo Martens pays it forward MacEwan University appoints deputy provost Office hours: How they changed Dr. Amanda Nelund’s life “Doing this work feels like coming home.” MacEwan welcomes new associate vice-president, Student Support and Accountability EXPLORE JOB OPPORTUNITIES Build your future today. We can't wait to grow with you. Pension, benefits & time away Balance & Well-Being Professional Development Working on Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
