    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.196": {
      "title": "Manager, Capital Planning and Asset Management",
      "description": "Manager, Capital Planning and Asset Management - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Manager, Capital Planning and Asset Management Financial Services Competition No. 26.08.196 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $95,144 to $128,623 per annum. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $95,144 to $128,623 per annum. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Manager, Capital Planning and Asset Management for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Financial Services department. The Manager, Capital Planning and Asset Management (CPAM) provides leadership and oversight of the University's capital planning, project accounting, and asset management functions. The position is responsible for the financial monitoring and analysis of major capital initiatives, including building projects, infrastructure renewals, and multi-year technology investments, as well as the lifecycle management of all capital and tracked non-capital assets. Key responsibilities include: Reporting, Regulatory Compliance & Financial Stewardship: Ensuring compliance with Public Sector Accounting Standards (PSAS), government reporting requirements, taxation requirements, and institutional policies; Developing and leading monthly, quarterly, annual, and ad hoc financial reporting related to capital projects, assets, and asset replacement planning; Managing audit requirements related to CPAM, responding to audit requests, and monitoring implementation of audit recommendations; Implementing, updating, and reviewing processes and quality assurance mechanisms to ensure the accuracy and integrity of CPAM financial reporting; Capital Planning, Projects & Asset Management: Providing financial leadership and analysis related to campus development plans, capital construction projects, infrastructure initiatives, and major technology investments; Being accountable for financial oversight, monitoring, analysis, and accuracy of major University capital projects; Providing oversight and guidance regarding project budgeting, financial monitoring, project reporting structures, and capital eligibility assessments; Accounting Operations, Systems Innovation & Internal Controls: Providing oversight of accounting practices, financial controls, and governance frameworks supporting capital projects, capital assets, and institutional asset management; Leading the modernization, optimization, and continuous improvement of processes and systems supporting capital planning, project accounting, and asset management functions; Establishing and maintaining effective internal controls, operating procedures, data governance standards, and risk management practices; Staff Leadership & Stakeholder Advisory: Leading, mentoring, and developing CPAM staff through a supportive leadership approach with oversight of service quality and work output; ensuring employees receive training, guidance, and support necessary to perform effectively; and Partnering with stakeholders across the University to identify emerging business needs, process inefficiencies, and operational challenges, and leading the development of practical process, business, and technology solutions that improve effectiveness, service delivery, and user experience. Skills You will have: Solid understanding of Public Sector Accounting Standards (PSAS) or International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS), including financial governance, regulatory compliance, and taxation requirements such as GST; Strong understanding of financial systems, data governance, reporting tools, and the application of technology to support decision-making, operational performance, and continuous improvement; Expertise in project accounting, asset lifecycle management, and internal control practices to ensure the effective management and stewardship of both capital and tracked non-capital assets; Strong stakeholder engagement, consultation, and relationship-management skills, with the ability to collaborate and influence internal and external stakeholders; Exceptional analytical and problem-solving abilities, with strong strategic thinking and decision-making skills; The ability to assess organizational risks, develop and implement mitigation plans, and establish effective controls and governance frameworks to support compliance, accountability and sound decision-making; The ability to evaluate business requirements and leverage process redesign, data analytics, and technology to develop practical, sustainable solutions that improve operational efficiency, data quality, service delivery and stakeholder experience; Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate complex financial and technical information to diverse audiences; Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to establish priorities, manage competing demands, and meet deadlines; The ability to work in a dynamic and fast-paced environment, especially during peak times of year; Strong attention to detail and accuracy of work; and Proven leadership skills with the ability to build high-performing teams, develop and implement KPIs, and foster a culture of continuous improvement and innovation. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor of Commerce degree with a major in Accounting or a related degree. Chartered Professional Accountant (CPA) designation. A minimum of 8 years of progressively responsible accounting, financial analysis, or asset management experience. A minimum of 3 years of leadership experience. Experience with Public Sector Accounting Standards (PSAS) or International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS). Experience with capital planning, financial oversight, and project governance of major building, infrastructure, and multi-year technology projects. Experience leading process improvement initiatives and technology-enabled solutions that enhance operational effective Experience working with enterprise financial systems; PeopleSoft experience would be considered an asset. Experience in post-secondary or public sector environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.219": {
      "title": "4th Class Power Engineer",
      "description": "4th Class Power Engineer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS 4th Class Power Engineer Facilities, Infrastructure and Planning Management Competition No. 26.09.219 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 25, 2026. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 25, 2026. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a 4 th Class Power Engineer for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Facilities department. The 4th Class Power Engineer will be responsible for operating and maintaining boilers, chillers, generators, and auxiliary equipment to provide heat, refrigeration, and other services for the university infrastructure. This position will also provide back-up services to the operation of the BMS (Building Management System), monitor and inspect heating plant equipment, switches, gauges, valves, alarms, meters, and perform some of the more technical tasks on HVAC servicing. Key responsibilities include: Daily inspecting of boilers, chillers and generators, including associated pumps, thermal exchange equipment and controls; Reviewing and recording gauges that measure temperature as well as pressure readings, while documenting all deficiencies noted to ensure plant equipment is operating at maximum efficiency; Troubleshooting and performing corrective action and minor repairs to prevent equipment or system failures; Performing minor HVAC repairs and replacing filters; Performing minor facility repairs such as architectural, plumbing, door hardware, calibrations, etc) repairs; Cleaning and lubricating generators, pumps and compressors, and perform other routine equipment maintenance duties using appropriate lubricants, hand, power, and precision tools; Maintaining mechanical areas in an acceptable condition; Maintaining a daily log of operation, maintenance and safety activities, and writing reports on plant operation and non-compliance; Monitoring hydronic heating and cooling system chemical treatment and recommending and overseeing corrective measures; and Preparing for and performing annual internal inspections of hot water equipment, boilers, tanks, pressure vessels and miscellaneous equipment, replacing pressure relief valves. Skills You will have: The ability to independently research, diagnose issues and initiate repairs with building heating and cooling systems; Working knowledge on understanding, applying, and utilizing mechanical principles and concepts in a commercial building setting; and Strong technical skills and knowledge using applicable tools, machinery, and mechanical systems. Qualifications A minimum of a High School diploma, with a current 4th Class Power Engineer certification. A minimum of 3 years of Power Engineer experience with commercial building operations or institutional settings. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only A valid Driver’s License Availability to work a shift from 1:00pm to 9:00pm Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. ​ ​ This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. ​ All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.212": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Academic Advisor Faculty of Arts and Science Competition No. 26.09.212 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 15, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 15, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University invites applicants for a full-time continuing Academic Advisor opportunity with our Faculty of Arts and Science. Reporting to the Associate Dean, Operations, you will support both the Bachelor of Arts (BA) and Bachelor of Science (BSc), programs, helping students in pursuing academic success at MacEwan University. Key responsibilities include: Communicating comprehensive knowledge regarding the BA degree and the BSc degree, as well as relevant MacEwan University policies and procedures; Developing information resources and processes and facilitating activities to support student recruitment, success, and retention; Providing information, advising, and support to students, parents/guardians, faculty, staff, and external contacts; and, Providing sensitive academic guidance to students faced with complex and/or emotional situations. Skills You will have: The ability to communicate effectively with diverse populations verbally and in writing, utilizing a variety of systems and tools; Strong problem-solving skills; Strong attention to detail, with the ability to prioritize and multi-task; The ability to work independently as well as the ability to develop and maintain effective working relationships; Strong presentation skills; The ability to learn and use a variety of computer applications. Experience with PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, Microsoft 365, and Google Suite is preferred; and, A keen interest in keeping up-to-date and leveraging teaching and learning applications is an asset, including learning management systems and database platforms. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree. A minimum of two years of experience in a post-secondary institution working with students. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.213": {
      "title": "Human Resources Business Partner",
      "description": "Human Resources Business Partner - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Human Resources Business Partner Human Resources Competition No. 26.09.213 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $84,387 to $113,923 per annum September 25, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $84,387 to $113,923 per annum Closing Date September 25, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity We are seeking a collaborative and relationship-focused Human Resources Business Partner (HRBP) to join our HR team. In this role, you will build trusted partnerships with leaders, foster open dialogue, navigate complex situations, and develop practical solutions with diverse stakeholders. You will embrace new challenges while bringing a thoughtful and innovative approach to addressing strategic, emerging people and organizational issues. Through your curiosity, sound judgment, and adaptability, you will help clients successfully navigate change and growth, in support of MacEwan University’s Teaching Greatness: Strategic Vision 2030 . Key responsibilities include: Forging trusted relationships with senior leaders, managers, subject matter experts, and HR shared services partners to provide strategic guidance, influence decision-making, and coordinate integrated approaches to complex people and organizational matters; Providing consultation and advice to leaders on a variety of strategic, operational, and complex HR initiatives, challenges, and solutions; Using a systems-thinking approach to identify current and future workforce needs, understand operational priorities, and develop or broker strategies and initiatives that support organizational objectives; Serving as a valued member of assigned leadership teams; applying an HR lens to business decisions and contributing to the achievement of departmental and institutional goals; Interpreting, applying, and ensuring compliance with collective agreements (MacEwan Staff Union and Grant MacEwan Faculty Association), the Out-of-Scope Handbook, University policies, and relevant legislation; Providing coaching, guidance, and support to managers on employee relations matters, including performance management, probationary reviews, and disciplinary processes; Acting as a change agent by supporting leaders through organizational change, including change management, transformation initiatives, and assisting with organizational design; Conducting workplace investigations and supporting grievance management processes, including facilitating investigations, preparing reports, providing recommendations, and supporting the implementation of outcomes; and Supporting talent acquisition activities by providing guidance and consultation throughout the recruitment and selection process. Skills You will have: Strong consultative mindset, able to ask insightful questions, understand business priorities, and translate organizational needs into practical and forward-thinking people solutions; The ability to effectively interact, communicate, influence, and collaborate with various partners and stakeholders, including senior management, staff at all levels, union representatives, and other organizations; The ability to create a culture of trust and transparency; Sound judgment and the ability to manage highly confidential and sensitive issues with solid business and political acumen; The ability to work within broad HR parameters and challenge the status quo in proposing strategies and programs to support sustained employee engagement; The proven ability to efficiently collect, analyze, integrate, and interpret complex information and data from diverse sources and viewpoints; Superior interpersonal skills and ability to effectively manage and lead work groups; Proven project management, portfolio planning, change leadership and organizational skills; and Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including report writing and presentation skills. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Arts, Business, Human Resources, Labour/Industrial Relations, or other related discipline. A minimum of 5 years of experience in a unionized workplace with more than 1 collective agreement. A minimum of 2 years of experience in resolving labour relations issues and formal grievance handling. Experience completing workplace investigations and preparing recommendations and reports. Experience in talent acquisition, including candidate sourcing. Experience in providing advice and strategic HR consulting services to senior-level management. Demonstrated experience implementing complex, strategic, institution-wide plans, programs, and initiatives. Experience managing multi-disciplinary projects that may be politically sensitive and complex. Experience developing and managing complex, multi-dimensional relationships. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.217": {
      "title": "Senior Analyst, IT Security Operations",
      "description": "Senior Analyst, IT Security Operations - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Analyst, IT Security Operations Information Technology Services Competition No. 26.09.217 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 18, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 18, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking multiple Senior Analysts, IT Security Operations for up to 2 full-time continuing opportunities with Information Technology Services. Reporting to the Senior Director, the Senior Analyst, IT Security Operations plays an important role in the implementation, operation, and ongoing support of secure and reliable information security technologies at MacEwan. The position completes complex technical analyses, develops and implements security controls and operational enhancements, and supports the monitoring, protection, and continuous improvement of the University’s technology environment. The role also supports cyber incident triage and response by investigating security alerts, assessing potential exposure, and supporting remediation in accordance with established incident response processes. Key responsibilities include: Leads technical work related to the implementation, operation, and continuous improvement of IT security applications, controls, and procedures, informed by audit findings, identified security gaps, and lessons learned from post-incident reviews; Develops and extends the University's security monitoring platforms to provide automated alerts which minimize the daily operational tasks within the Information Security department. Works with other areas of IT to improve their security posture through industry best practices and security orchestration, automation, and response (SOAR) methodologies; Designs, develops, and delivers the annual Cyber Security & Privacy Awareness training course, collaborating with the ITS Leadership and the Manager, Information & Privacy Office to ensure that regulatory and best practice training requirements for the University are met; Works with ITS Leadership, and IT staff, including systems administrators, network administrators, security operations, and security governance, risk, and compliance (GRC) team members to assess security issues, recommend remediation actions, and support follow-up with responsible technical teams; Supports and maintains the Information Technology Services vulnerability management processes by monitoring identified vulnerabilities, performing quarterly reviews to support PCI-DSS compliance requirements, ensuring that other IT areas are installing security patches and applying remediation security configurations for IT resources and that the University is properly monitoring these systems; and Remains current in industry trends and best practices across a broad range of information security disciplines, including software development security, security operations, security assessment and testing, identity and access management (IAM), security and risk management, asset security, security architecture and design, and communication and network security. Skills You will have: Passion, interest, and understanding of trends and best practices in information security and related technologies; Demonstrable IT skills such as working with enterprise technology environments and modern platforms such as cloud service providers and security software; Excellent communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with external stakeholders and internal stakeholders at varying levels within the organization and to translate technical concepts for non-technical audiences; Excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively and build/maintain strong working relationships; Strong planning and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple initiatives simultaneously; The ability to gather data, investigate, analyze, and synthesize information to draw conclusions and make recommendations; The ability to navigate situations that can be somewhat ambiguous with the ability to design solutions that work across platforms; Strong attention to detail and excellent organizational, time management, analytical, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills, enabling you to effectively manage priorities and deliver high-quality results; The ability to multitask, take initiative, demonstrate flexibility to adapt to changing situations and priorities, and meet critical deadlines; Experience with various computer networks, operating systems, software, hardware, and diverse operating systems and platforms such as: Linux, Windows, macOS, iPhone, Android, and cloud environments and service providers such as Microsoft Azure, Amazon Web Services (AWS), and Google Cloud; The ability to work independently and in a collaborative team environment; and Scripting knowledge (e.g., Python or PowerShell) to support the automation of workflows and connectors; experience with these tools would be considered an asset. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Information Systems or related field. Current Information Security certification, such as SSCP (Systems Security Certified Professional), Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP), Certified Cybersecurity Operations Analyst (CCOA), Offensive Security Certified Professional (OSCP) from ISC2, ISACA, OffSec, or similar body. A minimum of 7 years of progressive experience in Information Technology with at least 3 years of working experience with information security. Experience in leading projects with elements of change management and compliance. Demonstrated knowledge of security risk frameworks and incident response practices. Proven experience with information security operational and response technologies such as security incident and event management (SIEM), extended endpoint detection and response (XDR), security orchestration and automated response (SOAR), digital forensics incident response (DFIR). Experience working within a post-secondary or public sector environment is considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position may be required to work overtime, including occasional evening or weekend work to accommodate system maintenance or urgent user support. This position is required to be on-call in a rotational basis to support the 24×7 Information Technology Services On-Call & Escalation Process. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.216": {
      "title": "Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst, Campus Solutions",
      "description": "Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst, Campus Solutions - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst, Campus Solutions Information Technology Services Competition No. 26.09.216 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). September 22, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date September 22, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst for a full-time continuing opportunity with Information Technology Services. The Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst acts as a technical liaison between developers and business stakeholders and is responsible for gathering and analyzing business requirements related to enterprise applications and systems and producing detailed technical design specifications to address specific business needs. The role focuses on enterprise applications supporting admissions, enrolment, student records, curriculum management, academic scheduling, and related student services functions. Specializing in enterprise platforms that support the student lifecycle, academic scheduling, and institutional operations, this role provides analysis and solution design expertise for systems including PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, Infosilem Academic, Infosilem Campus, and associated integrations and third-party applications. The position works closely with stakeholders across the University, including the Office of the University Registrar and other administrative and academic business units to ensure technology solutions effectively support institutional processes and strategic objectives. When Functional Analysts or Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) encounter complex system challenges that go beyond standard configuration capabilities or require deeper technical expertise, the Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst will take ownership of the request. Acting as a bridge between business users and IT teams, the Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst evaluates escalated issues, determines whether custom development or integration is required, and ensures solutions align with both operational needs and technical feasibility. This role is also key in communicating requirements to either an internal development team or third-party developers for effort estimation and execution. As a key member of the Enterprise Applications team, the Senior Enterprise Solutions Analyst communicates requirements to internal development teams and third-party solution providers, supports effort estimation and roadmap planning, and helps ensure the long-term sustainability, reliability, and effectiveness of the university's enterprise student systems environment. Key responsibilities include: Conducting gap analysis between current and desired system functionalities; Analyzing and documenting business processes related to admissions, enrolment, student records, curriculum management, academic scheduling, and related institutional operations; Reviewing the existing IT environment to assess available technologies and determine necessary solution developments; Utilizing industry best practices to develop scalable and robust IT solutions, including system specifications, architecture diagrams, and wireframes; Developing solution prototypes and process models to validate requirements and gather stakeholder feedback; Providing technical expertise to business leaders and ITS members regarding system implementation and usage; Remaining current with technology and industry trends and best practices; researching, analyzing, and evaluating applicability and feasibility of new technologies, changes or enhancements to current technologies, and effects of new methodologies; Translating business requirements into technical specifications and collaborating with developers to implement solutions; and Developing and executing change management strategies for system integration initiatives. Skills You will have: A strong understanding of both business processes and technical systems; Proven experience with business analysis methodologies, frameworks, and tools; Strong knowledge and experience in requirements gathering, business process modeling, solution design, process improvement, and advanced data analysis; The ability to foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages innovation, teamwork and the sharing of knowledge; Strong stakeholder engagement skills, including relationship management and active listening; Strong negotiation and influencing skills with the ability to set and manage customer expectations; Excellent problem-solving and critical-thinking skills with a proactive approach; Strong analytical skills for system analysis and design with keen attention to detail; Effective communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to convey technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders; The ability to balance competing priorities and manage complex initiatives; The ability to work effectively within a team environment; Strong understanding of PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, Infosilem Academic, Infosilem Campus, Slate, and other enterprise software solutions supporting student administration and academic operations; and Proficiency in data analysis tools such as SQL, Excel and/or Power BI. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Business Analysis or a related field; A minimum of 5 years of progressive experience in enterprise solution analysis, software development, IT system design, or related roles; Experience with software development, systems integration, and technical architecture; Experience with process mapping, workflow design, and requirements gathering; Experience with PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, including Admissions, Campus Community, Curriculum Management, Student Records, Academic Advisement, and related student administration processes; Knowledge of Infosilem Academic, Infosilem Campus, CourseLeaf CAT/CIM, and Slate would be considered assets; Knowledge of SQL and the Campus Solutions database structure; Knowledge of PeopleSoft Development Tools (Application Designer, PeopleCode, SQR) would be considered an asset; Experience analyzing and supporting integrations between PeopleSoft Campus Solutions and third-party enterprise applications; Knowledge of cloud-based enterprise solutions and modern IT frameworks; Experience within a post-secondary institution would be considered an asset; and An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements The position may be required to participate in the ITS on-call schedule for after-hours support. The position may be required to work outside of normal operational hours (i.e., evenings and weekends) to support urgent issues if they arise. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.214": {
      "title": "Team Lead, Sourcing",
      "description": "Team Lead, Sourcing - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Team Lead, Sourcing Procurement and Contract Management Services Competition No. 26.09.214 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). October 2, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band G (Steps 1-8): $41.674 - $60.619 per hour. $75,846 - $110,326 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date October 2, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Team Lead, Sourcing for a full-time continuing opportunity within our Procurement and Contract Management Services.. The Team Lead, Sourcing provides strategic and operational leadership to the Procurement Sourcing Team, ensuring the effective delivery of competitive procurement processes and contract administration services. Reporting to the Director, this position provides a leadership/advisory role to the Sourcing Team related to low-, medium-, and high-risk/visibility/value procurement & contract administration services. Key responsibilities include: Performing risk assessments on potential high-risk competitive bids and agreements and ensuring appropriate mitigating strategies are incorporated into procurement planning; Leading and managing complex, high value contracts, including overseeing contract changes, performance obligations, and commercial risk management; Leading complex negotiations for high-risk procurements, interpreting contractual requirements, anticipating required changes, facilitating consensus among stakeholders, and ensuring outcomes align with institutional and legal obligations; Providing stewardship over procurement and contract administration processes for the acquisition of goods and services on behalf of MacEwan University, ensuring they support institutional objectives and adhere to governance frameworks; Analyzing procurement and spend data to develop reports evaluating cost and service effectiveness, supplier performance, market conditions, and process improvements. Reporting to Director on cost control, supply risks, internal customers relations, performance checks, processes improvements, sourcing projects, and strategic collaborations; Acting as a primary Administrator for external sourcing platforms (e.g., Euna/Bonfire), managing template standardization and system workflows, actively monitoring external procurement portals and platforms to ensure posting accuracy and compliance with public-sector disclosure requirements; Monitoring supplier performance and collaborating with stakeholders to address issues, implement corrective actions, and support continuous improvement; Providing ongoing coaching and mentoring to unit staff leveraging expert knowledge of procurement strategies, trade agreements, policies, procedures, and contract law, supporting both technical development and professional growth; Identifying opportunities for process and service improvements, recommending and supporting implementation initiatives, and proactively identifying, assessing, and escalating operational, compliance, and service quality risks; and Providing full supervisory oversight for the Procurement Sourcing Team, including participating in recruitment, onboarding, training, providing positive and constructive coaching, employee development, performance coaching, and escalating matters to the Director as appropriate to ensure operational effectiveness and alignment with work performance expectations. Skills You will have: Comprehensive knowledge of procurement policies, procedures, and supply management strategies and techniques; Knowledge of contract and competitive bid law, and understanding of legal language related to contracts and agreements; The ability to communicate issues to a wide range of audiences, including Executive Officers; Demonstrated skills in negotiations and relationship building; The ability to develop consensus and influence resolution; Extensive knowledge of negotiations as they relate to contracting and subcontracting; Strong understanding of the post-secondary institution environment or a large complex organization; Strong management and leadership skills including a demonstrated ability to lead team members in a service-oriented and client-centered environment; multi-tasking and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks; Strong organizational and detailed-oriented skills; Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills; The ability to work calmly and effectively under pressure to meet deadlines; A positive and self-motivated attitude; The ability to communicate effectively with internal and external stakeholders, both written and verbal; The ability to manage large and complex projects; Strong understanding of the current marketplace to manage stakeholder requirements; and Excellent interpersonal skills. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor's degree in Business, Commerce, or a related field. A professional certification in the supply management field (Supply Chain Management Professional (SCMP) designation), or equivalent. A minimum of 7 years’ related procurement experience, including leading high-risk end-to-end competitive bids, leading contract negotiations, contract administration (draft and execution), contract management, performing diversified supply chain management, leading teams, and overseeing procurement operations. Experience within a public sector institution or a large organization would be considered an asset. Comprehensive knowledge of trade agreements (e.g., New West Partnership Trade Agreement (NWPTA), Canadian Free Trade Agreement (CFTA)) would be considered an asset. Working knowledge of relevant software and systems such as Euna Procurement (aka Bonfire), Google workplace, MS Office, Contract Lifecycle Management software, E-Procurement Solutions, E-Signature software, and PeopleSoft applications would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.222": {
      "title": "Advisor, Procurement and Contracts",
      "description": "Advisor, Procurement and Contracts - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Advisor, Procurement and Contracts Procurement and Contract Management Services Competition No. 26.09.222 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week). MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week).​ October 12, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week). Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week).​ Closing Date October 12, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Advisor, Procurement and Contracts for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Procurement and Contract Management Services. The Advisor, Procurement and Contracts is responsible for leading assigned end-to-end low to medium-risk, low to medium-visibility, and/or low to medium-value procurement and contract services to meet the widely varying needs of the stakeholders across the university. Key responsibilities include: Planning and Research Conducting regular meetings with internal stakeholders to understand procurement and business requirements; and Completing market research, procurement background assessment, and recommending procurement and contracting strategies to best meet business objectives with leadership support. Competitive Bidding and Contract Administration Providing procurement and contract advice to various MacEwan’s stakeholders while working closely with MacEwan's legal department for expertise; Full ownership of the bidding process, which includes document development, solicitation on Alberta Purchasing Connection (APC), evaluation,  awards on APC, regrets, and debriefs while ensuring proper stakeholder engagement, Leading end-to-end low to medium-risk, low to medium-visibility, and/or low to medium-value RFx processes; Sporadic involvement in high value/risk/visibility contracts and competitive bids under supervision, or in a supporting role to Procurement Senior Advisors; Leading and facilitating debriefing of unsuccessful bidders toward improvement of future responses and, based on feedback received, improvement of future competitive bidding documents.; Interpreting contract requirements, terms & conditions, and ensuring that all parties understand their responsibilities; and Facilitating and managing internal and external stakeholders’ engagement during the competitive bid and contract administration. Departmental and Business Support Acting as a liaison between internal stakeholders and suppliers as needed; and Diligently moving the business forward by suggesting process improvements, mitigating risks to the university, and containing costs. Skills You will have: Exceptional attention to detail; The ability to identify risks and propose strategies to mitigate same in the contracting process; Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and projects; Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written; Strong interpersonal, analytical and organizational skills; Demonstrated ability to deliver services in a service-oriented and client-centered environment; High level skill in using computers including experience with standard business applications including Microsoft Office and Excel; Demonstrated ability to work as a strong contributor in a team environment and able to effectively interact with all levels of management and staff; Experience with Contract Management Database, preferably PeopleSoft FSCM modules such as e-procurement, procurement, and PO Contract; Knowledge of relevant legislation and trade agreements with respect to public procurement obligations; Knowledge and experience in applying principles of project management; and Knowledge of contract laws. Qualifications A minimum of a post-secondary certification in a business-related field. A minimum of 5 years' related procurement experience. A minimum of 3 years supporting competitive bid processes, writing resultant contracts based on an existing contract template. Experience working in post-secondary institutions or public procurement would be considered an asset. Experience using MS Access, SharePoint, Visio, and / or Project. Formal training in Business (contract law) or public procurement would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. ​ ​ This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. ​ All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    }
